spec:
  grid: 15-17 rows x 16-18 cols, black background
  foreground: only red pixels; each 4-connected component is either a single pixel (area 1) or a domino (area 2, horizontal or vertical)
  objects:
    total: 9-23
    singles: 8-18
    dominoes: 1-5, at least 1 required
    orientation: mix of horizontal and vertical dominoes [observed]
  density: red pixels occupy 3-10% of grid cells [observed]
  separation: all red objects are 4-disconnected (guaranteed by definition); min Chebyshev distance between objects >= 1; objects may be diagonally adjacent
  transform:
    - preserve all input pixels
    - for each domino, expand its bounding box by 1 cell in every direction (clipped to grid edges)
    - paint green on the perimeter of that expanded box wherever the cell is currently black
    - single red pixels remain unframed
  output_colors: black + red + green; green only appears on expanded domino borders

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct random placement (input-first); transform is additive and non-destructive
  steps:
    1. pick grid size uniformly in 15-17 rows x 16-18 cols
    2. choose domino count D in 1-5 and single count S in 8-18
    3. place D dominoes one at a time; for each, pick random orientation (H/V), pick a random position, ensure all cells of the domino are black and the domino is 4-disconnected from all previously placed red pixels (Manhattan >= 2 from any existing red pixel)
    4. place S single red pixels one at a time; each must be 4-disconnected from all existing red pixels (Manhattan >= 2, i.e. no 4-adjacent red neighbor); Chebyshev >= 1 suffices
    5. verify at least 1 domino was placed
